# TODO(cloud-run-instances): Cloud Run Instances are Pre-GA and have no
# stable Terraform resource in hashicorp/google or google-beta as of 2026-09-02.
#
# Do NOT fake this with google_cloud_run_v2_service. The control plane's
# InstanceRuntime adapter (packages/cloud-run-instance-client) calls the
# REST API directly:
#   POST /v1/projects/{project}/locations/{region}/instances
#   POST /v1/projects/{project}/locations/{region}/instances/{id}:start
#   POST /v1/projects/{project}/locations/{region}/instances/{id}:stop
#
# When a resource ships (e.g. google_cloud_run_instance or
# google_cloud_run_v2_instance), rename this file to run_instances.tf and
# implement the instance definition. Baseline config per spec §22:
#   cpu: 4, memory: 8Gi, restartPolicy: ON_FAILURE, sandboxLauncher: true
#
# Track provider issues at:
#   https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-google/issues
